# monitor.conf — reference / example for the runtime monitor config.
#
# The real file lives at ~/.config/zovwm/monitor.conf and is written by
# the first-run monitor setup wizard (see the "Monitor setup wizard"
# section of the README) — you normally never hand-write this file, but
# it's plain text, so hand-editing works too. Editing this copy does
# nothing; only ~/.config/zovwm/monitor.conf is read.
#
# Format: one output per line —
#
#   output mode rate
#
# "output" is the RandR output name (`xrandr` lists them, e.g. eDP-1,
# HDMI-1, DP-2). "mode" is a resolution as WIDTHxHEIGHT. "rate" is the
# refresh rate in Hz, rounded to the nearest whole number. Each line is
# applied as `xrandr --output <output> --mode <mode> --rate <rate>` on
# every zovwm startup, and again on reload (Super+Shift+r or saving the
# file). Delete this file (the real one, in ~/.config/zovwm/) to see the
# monitor wizard again on the next login.

eDP-1 1920x1080 60

# A second output, e.g. an external monitor plugged into a laptop:
# HDMI-1 2560x1440 144
